{
 "script_name": "markov nested",
 "notes": [
  "The engine has no random step, so the drive cycle is a fixed Markov-style sequence of load states (idle 0.05, low 0.2, cruise 0.4-0.5, accel 0.6-0.8, peak 1.0 A/cm2), repeated 3 times by a matrix loop on CountA. About 7.5 min per cycle, 23 min total.",
  "Nested loop (2 levels): inside the CountA matrix loop, the 'Stop-and-go traffic' row calls the PostStep 'Stop and go', which loops 5 times on CountB (ramp to 0.3 A/cm2 in 3 s, hold 10 s, ramp to idle in 2 s, hold 8 s). Matrix loops can't be nested, so the inner loop lives in the PostStep.",
  "Short ramps (2-8 s) on LB_CURRENT_DENSITY_SP stand in for acceleration and braking.",
  "There is no cell-area or stoichiometry tag, so flows are fixed: 0.5/1.5 slpm H2/air during startup, 1.0/3.0 slpm during the drive cycle. That gives roughly 2.9x H2 and 3.6x air stoichiometry at 1.0 A/cm2 on a 25 cm2 cell, but only about 1.4x / 1.8x on a 50 cm2 cell. Check this against your cell area before running.",
  "Heat-up and cool-down use 1350 s ramps (45 degC at the 2 degC/min limit).",
  "LB_ENBL is turned ON only after both flows are above 0, and turned OFF before the flows go to 0 (LB_ENBL interlock).",
  "Startup aborts with an error if open-circuit voltage does not reach 0.85 V within 300 s.",
  "On the accel and peak rows, a Conditional drops the load to idle if LB_VOLTAGE_FB falls below 0.35 V."
 ],
